(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the built-in potential \(contact potential\) and depletion layer width of an abrupt PN junction from Poisson's equation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Abrupt PN Junction Electrostatics and Built-in Potential:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Equilibrium and Carrier Diffusion:) Tj
T*
(   - When P-type and N-type semiconductors are brought into metallurgical contact, majority holes) Tj
T*
(   diffuse from P to N, and majority electrons diffuse from N to P.) Tj
T*
(   - Uncompensated ionized acceptor dopants \(-q*Na\) remain fixed in the P-side, and ionized donors) Tj
T*
(   \(+q*Nd\) in the N-side, establishing a space charge \(depletion\) region and an internal electric) Tj
T*
(   field opposing further diffusion.) Tj
T*
(   2. Built-in Potential \(Vbi\) Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - At thermal equilibrium, net hole current is zero: J_p = J_p,drift + J_p,diffusion = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - q * p * mu_p * E - q * D_p * \(dp/dx\) = 0 => mu_p * E = D_p * \(1/p\) * \(dp/dx\).) Tj
T*
(   - Using Einstein relation D_p / mu_p = Vt = \(k*T\)/q, and electric field E = - dV/dx:) Tj
T*
(   - dV/dx = Vt * \(1/p\) * \(dp/dx\) => - dV = Vt * \(dp / p\).) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating across depletion region from x = -xp \(P-bulk, potential 0, p = pp0 approx Na\) to) Tj
T*
(   x = xn \(N-bulk, potential Vbi, p = pn0 = ni^2 / Nd\):) Tj
T*
(   Integral_0^{Vbi} \(-dV\) = Vt * Integral_{Na}^{ni^2/Nd} \(dp / p\).) Tj
T*
(   - Vbi = Vt * ln\( \(ni^2 / Nd\) / Na \) = - Vt * ln\( \(Na * Nd\) / ni^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   Vbi = Vt * ln[ \(Na * Nd\) / ni^2 ].) Tj
T*
(   3. Depletion Layer Width \(W\) from Poisson's Equation:) Tj
T*
(   - One-dimensional Poisson's equation: d^2 V / dx^2 = - rho\(x\) / \(epsilon_s\).) Tj
T*
(   - Charge neutrality requires: q * Na * xp = q * Nd * xn.) Tj
T*
(   - Integrating Poisson's equation across space charge region and applying boundary conditions:) Tj
T*
(   W = xn + xp = sqrt\( [ 2 * epsilon_s * \(Vbi - V_applied\) / q ] * [ \(Na + Nd\) / \(Na * Nd\) ] \).) Tj
T*
(   - Under forward bias \(V_applied > 0\), W narrows; under reverse bias \(V_applied = -Vr\), W) Tj
T*
(   widens.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast Zener Breakdown and Avalanche Breakdown mechanisms, highlighting doping levels, electric fields, and temperature coefficients.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Zener versus Avalanche Breakdown in PN Junctions:) Tj
T*
(   1. Zener Breakdown \(Direct Quantum Mechanical Tunneling\):) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Mechanism: Occurs in heavily doped PN junctions \(Na, Nd > 10^18 cm^-3\). Heavy doping) Tj
T*
(   compresses the depletion layer to an ultra-thin barrier \(< 10 nm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Under reverse bias, the valence band on the P-side aligns energetically with the empty) Tj
T*
(   conduction band on the N-side.) Tj
T*
(   - The intense electric field \(> 10^6 V/cm\) exerts sufficient electrostatic force to pull) Tj
T*
(   valence electrons directly across the thin forbidden gap into the conduction band via Quantum) Tj
T*
(   Mechanical Tunneling.) Tj
T*
(   - Breakdown Voltage: Typically occurs at low reverse voltages \(< 5-6 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Temperature Coefficient: Negative. As temperature rises, thermal energy reduces bandgap Eg,) Tj
T*
(   facilitating tunneling at lower reverse voltages: dVz / dT < 0.) Tj
T*
(   2. Avalanche Breakdown \(Impact Ionization Multiplication\):) Tj
T*
(   - Physical Mechanism: Occurs in lightly doped PN junctions with wide depletion regions.) Tj
T*
(   - Thermally generated minority carriers entering the depletion region are accelerated by the) Tj
T*
(   reverse electric field.) Tj
T*
(   - When carrier kinetic energy exceeds ionization threshold \(E_kin > 1.5 * Eg\), collisions with) Tj
T*
(   lattice atoms shatter covalent bonds, creating new electron-hole pairs \(Impact Ionization\).) Tj
T*
ET

