(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the Ripple Factor, Rectification Efficiency, and Peak Inverse Voltage \(PIV\) for a Full-Wave Bridge Rectifier.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Full-Wave Bridge Rectifier Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Circuit Operation:) Tj
T*
(   - Four diodes arranged in bridge configuration across AC secondary voltage v\(t\) = Vm *) Tj
T*
(   sin\(omega * t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Positive Half-Cycle: D1 and D2 conduct in series through load RL; D3 and D4 are reverse) Tj
T*
(   biased. Output voltage vo\(t\) = v\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Negative Half-Cycle: D3 and D4 conduct through RL in the identical current direction; D1 and) Tj
T*
(   D2 are reverse biased. Output voltage vo\(t\) = -v\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   2. DC \(Average\) Output Voltage and Current:) Tj
T*
(   - Idc = \(2 / pi\) * Integral_0^pi Im * sin\(theta\) d\(theta\) = 2 * Im / pi approx 0.6366 * Im.) Tj
T*
(   - Vdc = Idc * RL = \(2 * Vm / pi\).) Tj
T*
(   3. RMS Output Current:) Tj
T*
(   - Irms = sqrt\( \(1 / pi\) * Integral_0^pi Im^2 * sin^2\(theta\) d\(theta\) \) = Im / sqrt\(2\) approx) Tj
T*
(   0.7071 * Im.) Tj
T*
(   4. Ripple Factor \(r\):) Tj
T*
(   - Defined as ratio of RMS value of AC ripple components \(Iac\) to DC value \(Idc\):) Tj
T*
(   Iac = sqrt\( Irms^2 - Idc^2 \).) Tj
T*
(   r = Iac / Idc = sqrt\( \(Irms / Idc\)^2 - 1 \).) Tj
T*
(   r = sqrt\( [ \(Im / sqrt\(2\)\) / \(2 * Im / pi\) ]^2 - 1 \) = sqrt\( \(pi^2 / 8\) - 1 \) = sqrt\( 1.2337 -) Tj
T*
(   1 \) = sqrt\(0.2337\) approx 0.482 \(48.2%\).) Tj
T*
(   5. Maximum Theoretical Efficiency \(eta\):) Tj
T*
(   - DC output power: Pdc = Idc^2 * RL = \(2 * Im / pi\)^2 * RL = \(4 / pi^2\) * Im^2 * RL.) Tj
T*
(   - Total AC input power: Pac = Irms^2 * \(rf + RL\) = \(Im / sqrt\(2\)\)^2 * \(rf + RL\) = \(Im^2 / 2\) *) Tj
T*
(   \(rf + RL\).) Tj
T*
(   - Neglecting diode forward resistance rf:) Tj
T*
(   eta = Pdc / Pac = [ \(4 / pi^2\) * Im^2 * RL ] / [ \(1 / 2\) * Im^2 * RL ] = 8 / pi^2 approx 0.812) Tj
T*
(   \(81.2%\).) Tj
T*
(   6. Peak Inverse Voltage \(PIV\):) Tj
T*
(   - At peak AC voltage Vm, two non-conducting diodes share the reverse voltage: PIV = Vm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
