(   - Load current: IL = Vz / RL.) Tj
T*
(   - By KCL at output node: Is = Iz + IL => Iz = Is - IL.) Tj
T*
(   3. Design Bounds for Regulation:) Tj
T*
(   - To maintain regulation, Zener diode must remain in breakdown: Iz >= Iz_min \(knee current,) Tj
T*
(   typically 1-5 mA\).) Tj
T*
(   - To prevent thermal destruction, Zener current must not exceed maximum rated current: Iz <=) Tj
T*
(   Iz_max = Pz_max / Vz.) Tj
T*
(   4. Determining Limits of Series Resistor Rs:) Tj
T*
(   - Case 1: Minimum Input Voltage Vin_min and Maximum Load Current IL_max:) Tj
T*
(   Zener current is at minimum: Iz_min = Is - IL_max = [ \(Vin_min - Vz\) / Rs_max ] - IL_max.) Tj
T*
(   Rs_max = \(Vin_min - Vz\) / \(Iz_min + IL_max\).) Tj
T*
(   - Case 2: Maximum Input Voltage Vin_max and Minimum Load Current IL_min:) Tj
T*
(   Zener current is at maximum: Iz_max = [ \(Vin_max - Vz\) / Rs_min ] - IL_min.) Tj
T*
(   Rs_min = \(Vin_max - Vz\) / \(Iz_max + IL_min\).) Tj
T*
(   - The selected resistor must satisfy: Rs_min <= Rs <= Rs_max.) Tj
