(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the physical operation of an NPN Bipolar Junction Transistor in Active Mode, deriving carrier currents.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Physical Operation and Carrier Transport in NPN BJT \(Active Mode\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Biasing Conditions:) Tj
T*
(   - Emitter-Base Junction \(EBJ\): Forward biased \(Vbe approx 0.7 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - Collector-Base Junction \(CBJ\): Reverse biased \(Vcb > 0 V\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Emitter Injection and Base Transport:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Electron Injection\): Forward-biased EBJ lowers the potential barrier. Heavily doped) Tj
T*
(   n+ emitter injects a massive stream of electrons across the junction into the p-type base,) Tj
T*
(   forming emitter electron current InE. Simultaneously, a tiny hole current IpE is injected from) Tj
T*
(   base into emitter.) Tj
T*
(   Total emitter current: Ie = InE + IpE.) Tj
T*
(   Emitter injection efficiency: gamma = InE / \(InE + IpE\) approx 0.995.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Base Transit\): The p-base is deliberately engineered to be lightly doped and) Tj
T*
(   extremely narrow \(Wb << Ln, electron diffusion length\). Injected minority electrons diffuse) Tj
T*
(   across the base. Only a tiny fraction \(~0.5-1%\) recombine with majority holes in the base \(base) Tj
T*
(   recombination current I_B_rec\).) Tj
T*
(   Base Transport Factor: beta_T = InC / InE approx 0.995.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Collector Collection\): Electrons reaching the edge of the reverse-biased CBJ) Tj
T*
(   encounter a strong electric field sweeping downward toward the n+ collector. Electrons are) Tj
T*
(   rapidly swept into the collector, forming collector current InC.) Tj
T*
(   3. Total Collector Current:) Tj
T*
(   - Ic = InC + I_CBO = \(beta_T * gamma\) * Ie + I_CBO = alpha * Ie + I_CBO,) Tj
T*
(   where I_CBO is the reverse saturation current of the reverse-biased CBJ, and alpha = beta_T *) Tj
T*
(   gamma approx 0.98 - 0.998.) Tj
T*
(   4. Base Current:) Tj
T*
(   - By KCL: Ib = Ie - Ic = \(1 - alpha\) * Ie - I_CBO.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
