(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain BJT Biasing: Derive the Stability Factor S for Fixed Bias and Voltage Divider Bias circuits.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   BJT Biasing and Stability Factor Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition of Stability Factor S:) Tj
T*
(   - Quantifies thermal stability against collector leakage current drift:) Tj
T*
(   S = d\(Ic\) / d\(Ico\) |_{beta, Vbe = const}.) Tj
T*
(   - General relation derived from Ic = beta * Ib + \(1 + beta\) * Ico:) Tj
T*
(   Differentiating with respect to Ic:) Tj
T*
(   1 = beta * \(d\(Ib\)/d\(Ic\)\) + \(1 + beta\) * \(d\(Ico\)/d\(Ic\)\) = beta * \(d\(Ib\)/d\(Ic\)\) + \(1 + beta\) / S.) Tj
T*
(   S = \(1 + beta\) / [ 1 - beta * \(d\(Ib\) / d\(Ic\)\) ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Fixed Bias Circuit:) Tj
T*
(   - Base circuit KVL: Vcc = Ib * Rb + Vbe => Ib = \(Vcc - Vbe\) / Rb.) Tj
T*
(   - Since Ib is independent of Ic: d\(Ib\) / d\(Ic\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Stability Factor:) Tj
T*
(   S_fixed = 1 + beta.) Tj
T*
(   - For beta = 100: S = 101 \(Extremely poor thermal stability; prone to catastrophic thermal) Tj
T*
(   runaway\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Voltage Divider Bias \(Self-Bias Circuit\):) Tj
T*
(   - Thevenin equivalent of base divider \(R1, R2\):) Tj
T*
(   Vth = Vcc * [ R2 / \(R1 + R2\) ], and Rth = R1 || R2 = \(R1 * R2\) / \(R1 + R2\).) Tj
T*
(   - Base loop KVL with emitter resistor Re:) Tj
T*
(   Vth = Ib * Rth + Vbe + Ie * Re = Ib * Rth + Vbe + \(Ib + Ic\) * Re.) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiating with respect to Ic:) Tj
T*
(   0 = \(d\(Ib\)/d\(Ic\)\) * Rth + [ \(d\(Ib\)/d\(Ic\)\) + 1 ] * Re => \(d\(Ib\)/d\(Ic\)\) * \(Rth + Re\) = - Re.) Tj
T*
(   d\(Ib\) / d\(Ic\) = - Re / \(Rth + Re\).) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
