(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Thermal Runaway in a BJT and derive the mathematical condition to prevent it.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Thermal Runaway in BJT Amplifiers:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Power dissipated at the collector-base junction: P_c approx Vce * Ic.) Tj
T*
(   - This power dissipation elevates the junction temperature Tj:) Tj
T*
(   Delta-Tj = Tj - Ta = theta * P_c, where theta is thermal resistance \(deg C / W\) and Ta is) Tj
T*
(   ambient temperature.) Tj
T*
(   - Leakage current Ico doubles every 10 deg C rise in Tj: Ico proportional to exp\(k * Tj\).) Tj
T*
(   - Higher Ico drives higher collector current Ic: Ic = beta * Ib + \(1 + beta\) * Ico.) Tj
T*
(   - Higher Ic increases collector power dissipation P_c = Vce * Ic.) Tj
T*
(   - If heat generation outpaces thermal dissipation, a regenerative positive feedback loop occurs) Tj
T*
(   \('Thermal Runaway'\), leading to junction melting and permanent transistor destruction.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Condition to Prevent Thermal Runaway:) Tj
T*
(   - For stable equilibrium, the rate of increase of heat generation with junction temperature) Tj
T*
(   must be less than the rate of thermal heat dissipation:) Tj
T*
(   d\(P_c\) / d\(Tj\) < 1 / theta.) Tj
T*
(   - Differentiating P_c = Vce * Ic with respect to Tj:) Tj
T*
(   d\(P_c\) / d\(Tj\) = Vce * \(d\(Ic\) / d\(Tj\)\) + Ic * \(d\(Vce\) / d\(Tj\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - In a CE circuit with collector resistor Rc: Vce = Vcc - Ic * Rc => d\(Vce\)/d\(Ic\) = - Rc.) Tj
T*
(   d\(P_c\) / d\(Ic\) = Vce - 2 * Ic * Rc.) Tj
T*
(   d\(P_c\) / d\(Tj\) = \(d\(P_c\) / d\(Ic\)\) * \(d\(Ic\) / d\(Tj\)\) = \(Vce - 2 * Ic * Rc\) * \(d\(Ic\) / d\(Tj\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since d\(Ic\)/d\(Tj\) > 0, stability requires:) Tj
T*
(   Vce - 2 * Ic * Rc < 0 => Vce < 2 * Ic * Rc.) Tj
T*
(   - Since Ic * Rc = Vcc - Vce:) Tj
T*
(   Vce < 2 * \(Vcc - Vce\) => 3 * Vce < 2 * Vcc => Vce < \(2/3\) * Vcc.) Tj
T*
(   - Conservative Criterion: If the Q-point is chosen such that Vce < Vcc / 2, thermal runaway can) Tj
T*
(   NEVER occur.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
