(   2. De Morgan's Second Theorem:) Tj
T*
(   - Statement: The complement of a logical product \(AND\) is equal to the logical sum \(OR\) of the) Tj
T*
(   complements:) Tj
T*
(   \(A . B\)' = A' + B'.) Tj
T*
(   - Proof via Truth Table:) Tj
T*
(   A | B | A.B | \(A.B\)' | A' | B' | A'+B') Tj
T*
(   0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1) Tj
T*
(   0 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1) Tj
T*
(   1 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 1 | 1) Tj
T*
(   1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0) Tj
T*
(   The columns \(A.B\)' and A'+B' match identically. Q.E.D.) Tj
T*
(   3. Significance in Digital Design:) Tj
T*
(   - Enables conversion of any AND-OR network into an all-NAND or all-NOR network.) Tj
T*
(   - Forms the mathematical foundation for bubble logic and circuit simplification.) Tj
