BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Prove that NAND and NOR are Universal Logic Gates by implementing NOT, AND, OR, and XOR gates using NAND only.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Universality of NAND Gate:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition:) Tj
T*
(   A universal gate is a logic gate that can synthesize any arbitrary Boolean logic function) Tj
T*
(   without requiring any other gate type.) Tj
T*
(   2. Implementation of Basic Gates using ONLY 2-input NAND Gates:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) NOT Gate \(Inverter\):) Tj
T*
(   - Tie both inputs of NAND gate together: Y = \(A . A\)' = A'.) Tj
T*
(   - Number of NAND gates: 1.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) AND Gate:) Tj
T*
(   - Follow a NAND gate with a NAND inverter: Y = \(\(A . B\)'\)' = A . B.) Tj
T*
(   - Number of NAND gates: 2.) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) OR Gate:) Tj
T*
(   - Invert both inputs using NAND inverters, then pass into a third NAND gate:) Tj
T*
(   Y = \(A' . B'\)' = \(A'\)' + \(B'\)' = A + B \(by De Morgan's Law\).) Tj
T*
(   - Number of NAND gates: 3.) Tj
T*
(   \(d\) NOR Gate:) Tj
T*
(   - Invert the output of the 3-NAND OR gate:) Tj
T*
(   Number of NAND gates: 4.) Tj
T*
(   \(e\) XOR Gate \(A ^ B = A'B + AB'\):) Tj
T*
(   - Gate 1: N1 = \(A . B\)') Tj
T*
(   - Gate 2: N2 = \(A . N1\)' = \(A . \(A.B\)'\)') Tj
T*
(   - Gate 3: N3 = \(B . N1\)' = \(B . \(A.B\)'\)') Tj
T*
(   - Gate 4: Y = \(N2 . N3\)' = A ^ B.) Tj
T*
(   - Number of NAND gates: Exactly 4.) Tj
T*
