(   2. K-Map Grid Construction:) Tj
T*
(   - Rows indexed by AB \(00, 01, 11, 10\); Columns indexed by CD \(00, 01, 11, 10\) in Gray code) Tj
T*
(   sequence.) Tj
T*
(   - Plot minterms '1' at cells 1, 3, 7, 11, 15.) Tj
T*
(   - Plot don't cares 'X' at cells 0, 2, 5.) Tj
T*
(   - Plot zeros '0' at remaining cells.) Tj
T*
(   3. Cell Grouping Strategy:) Tj
T*
(   - Notice column CD = 11: Cells 3, 7, 11, 15 are all 1s. This forms a complete 4-cell column) Tj
T*
(   Quad \(cells 3, 7, 11, 15\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inspect Row AB = 00: Cells 0 \(X\), 1 \(1\), 3 \(1\), 2 \(X\) form a 4-cell row Quad!) Tj
T*
(   - Can we combine row 00 and column 11 with other cells?) Tj
T*
(   Look at cells \(0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7\): Cells 0\(X\), 1\(1\), 2\(X\), 3\(1\), 5\(X\), 7\(1\) together with) Tj
T*
(   empty cells.) Tj
T*
(   Actually, consider the 4-cell column CD=11: Cells \(3, 7, 11, 15\) -> Group 1. Term: C . D.) Tj
T*
(   Consider the entire top row AB = 00 \(cells 0, 1, 2, 3\): All four cells are either 1 or X!) Tj
T*
