(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the design and operation of an 8-to-1 Multiplexer and demonstrate function implementation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   8-to-1 Multiplexer \(Data Selector\) Design:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - 8 Data Inputs \(D0 to D7\), 3 Select Lines \(S2, S1, S0\), 1 Active-Low Enable \(E'\), and 1 Output) Tj
T*
(   \(Y\).) Tj
T*
(   - Output Boolean Equation:) Tj
T*
(   Y = E' . [ D0.S2'.S1'.S0' + D1.S2'.S1'.S0 + D2.S2'.S1.S0' + D3.S2'.S1.S0 + D4.S2.S1'.S0' +) Tj
T*
(   D5.S2.S1'.S0 + D6.S2.S1.S0' + D7.S2.S1.S0 ].) Tj
T*
(   2. Implementing 4-Variable Function:) Tj
T*
(   - Implement F\(A, B, C, D\) = Sum_m\(1, 3, 4, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15\) using an 8-to-1 MUX.) Tj
T*
(   - Assign variables A, B, C to select lines S2, S1, S0 respectively.) Tj
T*
(   - Variable D is routed to data inputs D0 to D7:) Tj
T*
(   * ABC = 000 \(minterms 0, 1\): F=0 for m0, F=1 for m1 => D0 = D.) Tj
T*
(   * ABC = 001 \(minterms 2, 3\): F=0 for m2, F=1 for m3 => D1 = D.) Tj
T*
(   * ABC = 010 \(minterms 4, 5\): F=1 for m4, F=0 for m5 => D2 = D'.) Tj
T*
(   * ABC = 011 \(minterms 6, 7\): F=0 for m6, F=0 for m7 => D3 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   * ABC = 100 \(minterms 8, 9\): F=0 for both => D4 = 0.) Tj
T*
(   * ABC = 101 \(minterms 10, 11\): F=0 for m10, F=1 for m11 => D5 = D.) Tj
T*
(   * ABC = 110 \(minterms 12, 13\): F=1 for both => D6 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   * ABC = 111 \(minterms 14, 15\): F=1 for both => D7 = 1.) Tj
T*
(   - The entire 4-variable function is implemented using a single 8:1 MUX IC with zero external) Tj
T*
(   logic gates!) Tj
