(>> Solution to Question 14:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Carry Look-Ahead Adder \(CLA\), deriving carry generate and propagate equations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Carry Look-Ahead Adder \(CLA\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Limitation of Ripple Carry Adder:) Tj
T*
(   - In an n-bit ripple carry adder, carry bits propagate serially through each stage: t_delay = n) Tj
T*
(   * 2 * t_gate. For a 64-bit adder, delay is unacceptably sluggish.) Tj
T*
(   2. Carry Look-Ahead Concept:) Tj
T*
(   - Eliminates ripple carry delay by calculating all carry signals simultaneously in parallel) Tj
T*
(   using two auxiliary functions:) Tj
T*
(   * Carry Generate: Gi = Ai . Bi \(Stage i generates a carry regardless of carry-in\).) Tj
T*
(   * Carry Propagate: Pi = Ai ^ Bi \(Stage i propagates carry-in to carry-out\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Carry Expressions:) Tj
T*
(   - Ci+1 = Gi + Pi . Ci.) Tj
T*
(   - Unrolling for 4 stages:) Tj
T*
(   C1 = G0 + P0 . C0) Tj
T*
(   C2 = G1 + P1 . C1 = G1 + P1 . \(G0 + P0.C0\) = G1 + P1.G0 + P1.P0.C0) Tj
T*
(   C3 = G2 + P2.G1 + P2.P1.G0 + P2.P1.P0.C0) Tj
T*
(   C4 = G3 + P3.G2 + P3.P2.G1 + P3.P2.P1.G0 + P3.P2.P1.P0.C0.) Tj
T*
(   4. Speed Advantage:) Tj
T*
(   - Each carry signal depends ONLY on inputs A, B, and initial carry C0.) Tj
T*
ET

