(   [Problem Statement]: Compare CMOS and TTL logic families regarding propagation delay, power dissipation, fan-out, and noise margins.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparison of CMOS and TTL Logic Families:) Tj
T*
(   1. Technology:) Tj
T*
(   - TTL \(Transistor-Transistor Logic\): Utilizes NPN bipolar junction transistors and) Tj
T*
(   multi-emitter transistors.) Tj
T*
(   - CMOS \(Complementary MOS\): Utilizes complementary pairs of P-channel and N-channel MOSFETs.) Tj
T*
(   2. Power Dissipation:) Tj
T*
(   - TTL: High static power dissipation \(~1-10 mW per gate\) due to constant DC bias currents.) Tj
T*
(   - CMOS: Near-zero static power dissipation \(< 10 nW per gate\). Dynamic power proportional to C) Tj
T*
(   * V^2 * f.) Tj
T*
(   3. Fan-Out:) Tj
T*
(   - TTL: Limited to ~10 standard gates due to DC input drive current requirements \(I_IL\).) Tj
T*
(   - CMOS: Extremely high \(> 50 gates at low frequencies\) because MOSFET gates draw zero DC) Tj
T*
(   current \(infinite input impedance\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Noise Margins:) Tj
T*
(   - TTL: Moderate. High-level noise margin NM_H = 0.4 V; Low-level noise margin NM_L = 0.4 V.) Tj
T*
(   - CMOS: Superior. Noise margins equal ~30-40% of supply voltage Vdd \(e.g., NM = 1.5 V for Vdd =) Tj
T*
(   5 V\).) Tj
T*
(   5. Supply Voltage Range:) Tj
T*
(   - TTL: Rigid 5 V +- 5% \(4.75 V to 5.25 V\).) Tj
T*
(   - CMOS: Flexible wide range \(1.2 V to 15 V\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
