(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the working principle and characteristics of Light Emitting Diodes \(LED\) and Photodiodes.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Optoelectronic Semiconductor Devices \(LED and Photodiode\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Light Emitting Diode \(LED\):) Tj
T*
(   - Operating Principle: Forward-biased PN junction fabricated from direct bandgap semiconductors) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., GaAs, GaP, GaN, InGaN\).) Tj
T*
(   - Under forward bias, injected minority electrons recombine with holes across the bandgap,) Tj
T*
(   releasing excess energy directly as optical photons: E_photon = h * nu = Eg.) Tj
T*
(   - Wavelength: lambda = \(h * c\) / Eg = 1.24 / Eg \(in micrometers\). Direct bandgap materials) Tj
T*
(   ensure radiative recombination dominates over non-radiative phonon dissipation.) Tj
T*
(   2. Photodiode:) Tj
T*
(   - Operating Principle: Operates in Reverse Bias.) Tj
T*
(   - Photons with energy h*nu >= Eg incident on the depletion region excite valence electrons into) Tj
T*
(   the conduction band, generating electron-hole pairs \(Photoconductive Effect\).) Tj
T*
(   - The reverse electric field rapidly sweeps electrons to N-side and holes to P-side, generating) Tj
T*
(   a reverse photocurrent:) Tj
T*
(   I_photo = R_resp * P_optical, where R_resp is responsivity \(A/W\).) Tj
T*
(   - Highly linear response across wide dynamic range; used in optical fiber communication and) Tj
T*
(   photodetectors.) Tj
T*
