(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the operation of a Varactor Diode, deriving the junction capacitance formula under reverse bias.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Varactor Diode \(Varicap\) Theory:) Tj
T*
(   1. Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - A PN junction diode engineered to operate exclusively in reverse bias, behaving as a) Tj
T*
(   voltage-controlled variable capacitor.) Tj
T*
(   - The P-region and N-region act as conductive capacitor plates, while the depleted space charge) Tj
T*
(   region serves as a dielectric of permittivity epsilon.) Tj
T*
(   2. Junction Capacitance Derivation:) Tj
T*
(   - Transition capacitance: C_t = dQ / dVr = epsilon * A / W, where W is depletion width.) Tj
T*
(   - Depletion width: W = sqrt\( [ 2 * epsilon * \(Vbi + Vr\) / q ] * [ \(Na + Nd\) / \(Na * Nd\) ] \).) Tj
T*
(   - Capacitance Formula:) Tj
T*
(   C_t\(Vr\) = C_0 / [ 1 + Vr / Vbi ]^m.) Tj
T*
(   - Grading coefficient m:) Tj
T*
(   * m = 0.5 for abrupt \(step\) junctions.) Tj
T*
(   * m = 0.33 for linearly graded junctions.) Tj
T*
(   * m = 1.0 to 2.0 for hyper-abrupt junctions.) Tj
T*
(   3. Applications:) Tj
T*
(   - Electronic tuning in television/FM radio receivers, Voltage-Controlled Oscillators \(VCOs\),) Tj
T*
(   Phase-Locked Loops \(PLLs\), and RF parametric amplifiers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
