(   - Depletion width is extraordinarily narrow \(< 10 nm, approx 100 atomic layers\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Operating Characteristics and Negative Resistance:) Tj
T*
(   - Zero Bias: Fermi levels align; no net tunneling current.) Tj
T*
(   - Small Forward Bias \(0 to Vp ~ 50 mV\): Conduction electrons on N-side align with unoccupied) Tj
T*
(   states in valence band on P-side. Electrons tunnel directly through the barrier, producing high) Tj
T*
(   Peak Current Ip.) Tj
T*
(   - Increasing Forward Bias \(Vp to Vv\): As bias increases, valence band states drop below) Tj
T*
(   conduction band electrons. Available tunneling states decrease; current drops from Peak Ip to) Tj
T*
(   Valley current Iv.) Tj
T*
(   * Dynamic resistance: rd = dV / dI < 0 \(Negative Differential Resistance region!\).) Tj
T*
(   - Beyond Valley Voltage Vv: Conventional forward diffusion current takes over.) Tj
T*
(   3. Applications:) Tj
T*
(   - Ultra-high-speed switching circuits, microwave oscillators, and reflection amplifiers) Tj
T*
(   operating up to tens of Gigahertz.) Tj
