(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Priority Encoders, designing a 4-to-2 Priority Encoder with truth table and K-map minimization.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   4-to-2 Priority Encoder Design:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operational Concept:) Tj
T*
(   - A standard encoder produces unpredictable invalid outputs when two or more inputs are) Tj
T*
(   asserted simultaneously.) Tj
T*
(   - A Priority Encoder resolves collisions by asserting the binary code corresponding strictly to) Tj
T*
(   the highest-priority active input.) Tj
T*
(   2. Truth Table \(D3 has highest priority, D0 lowest; V is valid output flag\):) Tj
T*
(   D3 | D2 | D1 | D0 | Y1 | Y0 | V) Tj
T*
(   0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | X | X | 0) Tj
T*
(   0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1) Tj
T*
(   0 | 0 | 1 | X | 0 | 1 | 1) Tj
T*
(   0 | 1 | X | X | 1 | 0 | 1) Tj
T*
(   1 | X | X | X | 1 | 1 | 1) Tj
T*
(   3. Boolean Expression Derivation via K-Maps:) Tj
T*
(   - Output Y1:) Tj
T*
(   Y1 is HIGH when D3=1 OR \(D2=1 and D3=0\):) Tj
T*
(   Y1 = D3 + D2.) Tj
T*
(   - Output Y0:) Tj
T*
(   Y0 is HIGH when D3=1 OR \(D1=1 and D2=0 and D3=0\):) Tj
T*
(   Y0 = D3 + D2' . D1.) Tj
T*
(   - Valid Bit V:) Tj
T*
(   V = D3 + D2 + D1 + D0.) Tj
T*
