(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Ebers-Moll Model of a BJT and derive equations for terminal currents across all operating regions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Ebers-Moll Model for Bipolar Junction Transistors:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Basis:) Tj
T*
(   - A non-linear large-signal model representing the BJT as two ideal diode junctions coupled by) Tj
T*
(   dependent current sources.) Tj
T*
(   2. Governing Equations:) Tj
T*
(   - Emitter Current:) Tj
T*
(   Ie = I_ES * [ exp\(Vbe / Vt\) - 1 ] - alpha_R * I_CS * [ exp\(Vbc / Vt\) - 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Collector Current:) Tj
T*
(   Ic = alpha_F * I_ES * [ exp\(Vbe / Vt\) - 1 ] - I_CS * [ exp\(Vbc / Vt\) - 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   - Base Current:) Tj
T*
(   Ib = Ie - Ic.) Tj
T*
(   3. Reciprocity Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - alpha_F * I_ES = alpha_R * I_CS = Is \(Transistor saturation current\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Operation across Regimes:) Tj
T*
(   - Forward Active: Vbe > 0, Vbc <= 0. Reduces to standard active equations.) Tj
T*
(   - Saturation: Vbe > 0, Vbc > 0. Both diodes conduct; collector current is governed by external) Tj
T*
(   load circuit.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
