(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Static CMOS Inverter: Voltage Transfer Characteristic \(VTC\), noise margins, and propagation delay.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Static CMOS Inverter Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Complementary pull-up PMOS and pull-down NMOS network sharing common gate input and drain) Tj
T*
(   output.) Tj
T*
(   2. Voltage Transfer Characteristic \(VTC\):) Tj
T*
(   - Region A \(Vin < Vtn\): NMOS OFF, PMOS Linear -> Vout = Vdd.) Tj
T*
(   - Region B \(Vtn < Vin < Vsp\): NMOS Saturation, PMOS Linear -> Vout drops.) Tj
T*
(   - Region C \(Vin = Vsp\): Switching threshold; both transistors in saturation. High gain region.) Tj
T*
(   - Region D \(Vsp < Vin < Vdd - |Vtp|\): NMOS Linear, PMOS Saturation.) Tj
T*
(   - Region E \(Vin > Vdd - |Vtp|\): NMOS Linear, PMOS OFF -> Vout = 0 V.) Tj
T*
(   3. Noise Margins:) Tj
T*
(   - NM_H = V_OH - V_IH) Tj
T*
(   - NM_L = V_IL - V_OL) Tj
T*
(   - For symmetric inverter \(beta_n = beta_p\), Vsp = Vdd / 2, yielding maximal noise immunity) Tj
T*
(   \(~Vdd / 2\).) Tj
T*
(   4. Dynamic Power Dissipation:) Tj
T*
(   P = C_L * Vdd^2 * f_clk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
