(   Quine-McCluskey \(Tabular\) Logic Minimization:) Tj
T*
(   1. Purpose:) Tj
T*
(   - A rigorous algorithmic method for simplifying Boolean expressions without relying on visual) Tj
T*
(   inspection, making it optimal for computer-aided logic synthesis.) Tj
T*
(   2. Step-by-Step Procedure:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1: Group minterms by the count of 1s in their binary representation.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2: Compare minterms between adjacent groups differing by exactly one bit position;) Tj
T*
(   combine them into product terms with a '-' \(dash\) representing the eliminated variable.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3: Repeat matching until no further reductions are possible. Unmatched terms form Prime) Tj
T*
(   Implicants \(PIs\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4: Construct Prime Implicant Table. Rows represent PIs, columns represent original) Tj
T*
(   minterms.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 5: Identify Essential Prime Implicants \(columns with a single checkmark\).) Tj
T*
(   - Step 6: Select minimal remaining PIs to cover uncovered minterms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
