(   [Problem Statement]: Describe Semiconductor Photolithography and the Planar Process used in monolithic IC fabrication.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Planar Process in Monolithic IC Fabrication:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Steps:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Silicon Ingot Growth & Wafer Slicing: Czochralski crystal pulling produces pure) Tj
T*
(   single-crystal silicon wafers.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Thermal Oxidation: Growing a protective layer of silicon dioxide \(SiO2\) at ~1000 deg C in) Tj
T*
(   oxygen/steam.) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Photolithography: Coating with photosensitive polymer \(photoresist\), UV exposure through a) Tj
T*
(   photomask, and chemical development to pattern windows in the resist.) Tj
T*
(   \(d\) Chemical / Plasma Etching: Transferring pattern by etching exposed SiO2 down to the silicon) Tj
T*
(   substrate.) Tj
T*
(   \(e\) Doping \(Thermal Diffusion / Ion Implantation\): Introducing dopant atoms \(Boron, Phosphorus\)) Tj
T*
(   through SiO2 windows to create P and N regions.) Tj
T*
(   \(f\) Metallization: Sputtering aluminum or copper to interconnect transistors into complete) Tj
T*
(   integrated circuits.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
